Consider again the voltage X from 

Div. The distribution of X is characterized by the pdf in . An alternative characterization that is more directly related to probabilities associated with X is obtained from the following function:\begin{align*}
F(x) &= \Pr(X \leq x) = \int_{-\infty}^{x}f(y)~dy = \begin{cases}
0 &\text{for }x \leq 0, \\
\int_{0}^{x}\frac{dy}{(1+y)^2} &\text{for }x > 0
\end{cases} \\
&= \begin{cases}
0 &\text{for }x \leq 0, \\
1 - \frac{1}{1+x} &\text{for }x > 0.
\end{cases}
\end{align*}

So, for example, \Pr(X \leq 3) = F(3) = 3/4.

